Hello, everyone.

I leaned very heavily on the spoilers, and would like to thank the
authors for writing and (mostly :-) ) maintaining them.  With that out
of the way...

Hoody-Hoo!! 

[Grep jumps up and down and thrashes wildly in what only the most
charitable might call a 'dance']

The game went fairly smoothly.  I made some ODSM around level fifteen,
and by the time I got to the castle I had three magic lamps.  I never
used any of those wishes, but it was nice to know they were there.  I
did use wishes from the castle wand freely.

There were only a few sticky bits.  My quest nemesis  was quite a bit
tougher than I expected.  He killed me, in fact.  I am now a true
believer in amulets of life-saving.  I did eventually kill him and took
the Tsurugi of Muramasa.  I used that to clean out the castle (I went
through the back door with boots of levitation), but I decided that
Excalibur and a shield of reflection were better on balance.

I was also beheaded by a skeleton with the Vorpal blade. I zapped it
with some wands of fire and took the sword.  Since I didn't want to
leave that or the Tsurugi lying around, I ended up carrying them all the
way to the entrance to the elemental planes. 

There was another scary moment when I polymorphed into a Dragon.  I
thought I had identified every ring except teleport control.  I was
wrong.  I eventually returned to my normal form and uncursed the ring,
but I lost a +4 T-shirt and a +2 cloak of protection during the
transformation.  

I thought I was going to die on the astral plane since I couldn't get
away from Death.  I finally thought to use my stethoscope and discovered
he only had 24 hit-points! I killed him with one blow and didn't worry
about him after that.  In the mean time he drained me of 90 hp. Ouch.

I had to visit every altar before I found the right one. Somehow I ended
up fighting Death and Pesty before I left the foyer.  Hunger was a
pushover.  In fact, there was so much less opposition at the third altar
that it was almost anti-climactic...

But not quite!  Hoody-Hoo!

